+# Apple III storage regression tests
+
+Run `tests/apple3/run.sh` from Main. The test links the production shared
+`iigs_disk.cpp` and `iigs_fmt.cpp` to file and SPI shims, with ASan/UBSan enabled.
+It runs on macOS and Linux and does not require ROMs, copyrighted disk images,
+or a MiSTer. Fixtures are generated from deterministic byte patterns.
+
+Coverage includes Apple III S0/S1 floppies and S2/S3 read-only block assignments;
+DOS/ProDOS/2MG conversion equivalence; 10-bit sync and bitstream GCR round-trips;
+NIB address-field preservation; the ProDOS-order sector map pinned to block
+positions; SOS protection-key reconstruction only for an encrypted SOS.INTERP; full 16 KiB transfers; partial final reads;
+DSK/PO/2MG sector write-back saved block by block, with torn, damaged and
+mis-tracked sectors kept out of the source; read-only writes that leave both
+RAM and disk unchanged; native WOZ CRC,
+metadata guards, allocation bounds and persistent writes; archive/host/INFO/FLUX
+protection; invalid 2MG/WOZ rejection; and existing //e/IIgs behavior.
+
+The same executable can serialize the actual Main mount result to a separate
+WOZ file for a core simulator or a writable copy:
+
+```
+/tmp/mister-apple3-tests/storage_test --convert source.dsk copy.woz
+```
+
+This utility uses Main's converter. There is no independent test-only encoder.
